# Freyalise's Winds and a stun counter both replace the untap of a permanent that has both counters (CR 122.1d, 614.1a), and
# the permanent's controller chooses which applies (CR 616.1e); the other then no longer applies (CR 614.6, 616.1f). As in
# the scenario where Bot2 chooses the Winds, Bot1's Rapier Wit taps and stuns Bot2's Ornithopter, which gets a wind counter.
# Here Bot2 applies the stun counter first on turn four: one stun counter comes off and the wind counter stays. On turn six
# the Winds alone replace the untap, and on turn eight the Ornithopter untaps.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Freyalise's Winds
Mox Pearl
Mox Pearl
Rapier Wit
Island
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Freyalise's Winds.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rapier Wit.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Replace(stun counter)
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = (absent)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Wind = 1
[T6 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Wind = (absent)
[T8 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
